cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IC-EconGym in research, please cite the software release and, when applicable, the accompanying paper."
title: "IC-EconGym: An Input–Output-Constrained Multi-Agent Testbed for Semiconductor Industrial Policy and Supply-Chain Resilience"
type: software
version: "0.3.0"
authors:
  - given-names: "Jinhua"
    family-names: "Gu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-2310-6150"
# license describes the software Work only; see LICENSE_SCOPE.md for artifact exclusions.
abstract: >-
  IC-EconGym is a research testbed with 13 industrial-sector agents and one government agent,
  15 configured tasks, and input-output-constrained execution of orders, source-specific materials,
  capacity, rationing and fiscal actions. It supports conditional mechanism experiments, strategy
  comparison, learning-policy evaluation, robustness analysis and local external-validation cases.
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jinhua188/IC-EconGym"
url: "https://jinhua188.github.io/IC-EconGym/"
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - agent-based computational economics
  - input-output analysis
  - semiconductor supply chain
  - industrial policy
  - supply-chain resilience
  - reinforcement learning
  - economic world models
